Modifications made in this fork (AGPL-3.0 section 5(a)), first published
2026-10-30:

  - src/infra/ffmpeg_paths.py
        is_ffmpeg_binary_usable() now also accepts Mach-O binaries
        (thin 32/64-bit and universal/fat headers), so a Homebrew or
        static macOS ffmpeg is recognised as valid.

  - install-macos.command, run-macos.command            [new]
        Double-clickable launchers: virtualenv bootstrap with a Python
        3.11-3.13 interpreter, mirror/proxy aware dependency install,
        libvlc environment for VLC.app, version sanity checks.

  - README.md, README.en.md, docs/quickstart.md          [rewritten]
        Rewritten around macOS instead of Windows.

  - src/media/formats.py                                 [additive]
        IMAGE_EXTS / is_supported_image_path /
        is_supported_media_path. VIDEO_EXTS is unchanged, so no
        existing caller changes behaviour.

  - src/storage/image_lance_store.py                     [new]
        image_assets Lance table (schema, upsert, vector search,
        row scan, stats, delete). Lives beside the video tables and
        never reads or writes them.

  - src/services/image_understanding.py                  [new]
        Structured image description through the configured
        OpenAI-compatible VLM: caption + people[] + tags[], strict
        JSON with prose fallback, TCP reachability probe.

  - src/services/image_index_service.py                  [new]
        Image scan, incremental indexing (CLIP + optional VLM
        description), text / keyword / image search, status.

  - src/services/image_index_service.py                  [extended]
        index_images(root_for_path=...) so one batch can span several
        registered folders; list_indexed_images() for grid browsing;
        prune_missing_images() moved here from the CLI.

  - src/services/image_index_service.py                  [extended]
        Chinese query routing. has_cjk() / query_terms() split a Han
        query at stop characters into 2-4 char sliding windows;
        search_by_query() runs a literal scan over caption / path /
        tags first and only falls back to CLIP vectors when nothing
        matched. The bundled CLIP text tower is English-only, so a
        Chinese query used to embed to noise. English queries keep the
        pure semantic path unchanged.

  - scripts/image_index.py                               [extended]
        search now defaults to search_by_query(), so the CLI gets the
        same Chinese routing as the GUI.

  - src/services/image_index_service.py                  [extended]
        prune_missing_images() skips rows whose registered root is
        unreachable, so an unplugged external drive is not read as
        "every photo was deleted". Reported as skipped_offline and
        surfaced by the page.

  - scripts/image_index.py                               [new]
        CLI: add / remove / roots / scan / index / search /
        status / prune.

  - tests/test_image_library.py                          [extended]
        30 cases covering formats, description parsing, scanning,
        content ids, Lance read/write, keyword and people filters;
        plus 12 for Chinese fragment extraction, literal scoring and
        the search_by_query language routing.

  - ui/widgets/image_library_page.py                     [new]
        In-app photo library page: folder management, indexing with
        progress and cancel, virtualised thumbnail grid, detail pane,
        drag-and-drop, people filter.

  - ui/image_thumbs.py                                   [new]
        Disk thumbnail cache (~/.videoseek/cache/image_thumbs) plus an
        off-thread loader, so the grid never decodes originals.

  - ui/widgets/image_library_page.py                     [extended]
        Semantic search now calls search_by_query(); the model hint and
        the result line explain the Chinese routing, and a vector-only
        fallback is labelled as such instead of pretending the search
        matched.

  - ui/windows/gui.py                                    [modified]
        Registers one extra built-in nav page ("images", after the
        video library) and its sidebar button. No existing page,
        signal or controller changed.

  - ui/windows/gui_apply_texts.py, ui/windows/gui_tray.py [modified]
        Refresh the new page's labels on language switch; shut its
        workers down with the rest of the app.

  - src/app/i18n.py                                      [modified]
        Added the nav_images string (zh/en). No existing key changed.

  - ui/widgets/styles.py                                 [modified]
        Added QSS for #ImageRootsList (folder list) only.

  - tests/test_image_library_ui.py                       [new]
        19 cases: grid model, thumbnail cache, detail preview layout,
        browse and prune APIs.

  - docs/image-library.md                                [new]
        Image library: data model, in-app UI, retrieval modes, Chinese
        query routing, prompt boundaries, performance, limitations.

  - docs/macos-notes.md                                  [new]
        Platform notes, known deltas, troubleshooting, sync policy.

  - DEPLOY-macOS.md                                      [removed]
        Content merged into docs/macos-notes.md.

The image library is additive: it adds one Lance table, new modules, one nav
page and a handful of QSS rules. The video indexing, search, export, OCR and
Agent API paths are untouched, and deleting the image_assets table returns the
app to upstream indexing behaviour (the empty page stays). Beyond the ffmpeg
binary detection, no upstream function changed its behaviour; the GUI edits
above only add the new page. Windows-specific code paths, packaging scripts and
the installer pipeline are untouched and unsupported here.
